#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/id #uuid "3d38f3e0-4c27-5ac6-ac16-9c8f57e0000e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4327" :question/problem "Find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-1,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1,5,-2 \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos θ &= \\frac{a \\cdot b}{\\mid a \\mid \\mid b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{a_{x}b_{x} + a_{y}b_{y} + a_{z}b_{z}}{\\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2} + a_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{b_{x}^{2} + b_{y}^{2} + b_{z}^{2}}} \\\\\n&= (2 \\cdot 1 + (-1) \\cdot 5 + 1 \\cdot (-2))/(\\sqrt{2^{2} + (-1)^{2} + 1^{2}}\\sqrt{1^{2} + 5^{2} + (-2)^{2}}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6} \\cdot \\sqrt{30}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6} \\cdot \\sqrt{6} \\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{6} \\right) \\approx 111.9^\\circ\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/id #uuid "d6d1be58-7321-50ca-a47d-5e80d55277c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4328" :question/problem "Find $\\angle BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,-5)$, $B(-1,0,-4)$, and $C(5,1,1)$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\na = ⟨2,-1,-5⟩, b = ⟨ - 1, 0,-4⟩, c = ⟨5, 1, 1⟩\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote\n\n$$\n\\angle BAC = \\theta\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1278/Source/Images/3326328c02627ffa40dbcdf7cb16cc96.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= b - a \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 1, 0,-4⟩ - ⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 1, 1⟩ \\\\\nAC^(→) &= c - a \\\\\n&= ⟨5, 1, 1⟩ - ⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨3, 2, 6⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos θ &= (AB^(→) \\cdot AC^(→))/(\\mid AB^(→) \\mid \\mid AC^(→) \\mid) \\\\\n&= (-3 \\cdot 3 + 1 \\cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot 6)/(\\sqrt{(-3)^{2} + 1^{2} + 1^{2}}\\sqrt{3^{2} + 2^{2} + 6^{2}}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{11}\\sqrt{49}} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}} \\right) \\approx 92.5^\\circ\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/id #uuid "fb2df468-d70d-5300-8860-0cb729cb13c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5112" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle t, \\, -2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 6, \\, t \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4\n$$\n\n, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na \\cdot b &= -4 \\\\\nt \\cdot 6 + (-2) \\cdot t &= -4 \\\\\n6t - 2t &= -4 \\\\\n4t &= -4 \\\\\nt &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\na = ⟨ - 1,-2⟩, b = ⟨6,-1⟩\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos θ &= \\frac{a \\cdot b}{\\mid a \\mid \\mid b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{a_{x}b_{x} + a_{y}b_{y}}{\\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{b_{x}^{2} + b_{y}^{2}}} \\\\\n&= (-4)/(\\sqrt{(-1)^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{6^{2} + (-1)^{2}}) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5} \\cdot \\sqrt{37}} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{185}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left(-\\dfrac{4}{\\sqrt{185}} \\right) \\approx 107.1^\\circ\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea9de93e-d608-510c-9830-15000067a76a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{84.37}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269061} {:answer/id #uuid "82c97997-bef6-5b00-9dda-e6c2385e1de2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{71.25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269062} {:answer/id #uuid "7e22e2b5-f91f-5fc6-879b-ea7b9daca6f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79.41}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269063} {:answer/id #uuid "0a53b0c8-688c-5914-81ce-28f2f2bdbe3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{69.56}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269064} {:answer/id #uuid "beaf3c5d-a0ca-5e73-817e-ba012989875d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75.12}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "beaf3c5d-a0ca-5e73-817e-ba012989875d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75.12}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269065} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d44a01f-eb22-5eb0-9f4c-4dafddb5fdf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269060}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5453ef5-4b15-5cbd-af32-541aa54e44cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-101504" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{21}\\cdot \\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{546}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{546}})≈{75.12}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269066 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27bcfe70-6989-5359-9ab8-99a8be1e27c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269068} {:answer/id #uuid "d9fd197d-e501-5e43-8c1c-2232a6ef539c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269069} {:answer/id #uuid "b8f831b4-cf64-570c-b2d2-906e374febed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269070} {:answer/id #uuid "1f9ac76d-964b-5482-9d58-9e89c6296713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269071} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf1043e-f893-5baa-9db6-4c2fb8c3639b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9fd197d-e501-5e43-8c1c-2232a6ef539c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269069} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdaea567-3b0b-54de-9b16-a108031e4eff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269067}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af00a80e-1320-5335-a947-5ce3ede8cf57" :question/math-academy-id "q-101510" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(-4,3,1)$, $Q(-1,2,0)$, and $R(-10,5,3).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨-4,3,1⟩,\\,q=⟨-1,2,0⟩,\\,r=⟨-10,5,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩-⟨-4,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨-10,5,3⟩-⟨-4,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot (-6)+(-1)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-22}{\\sqrt{11}\\cdot \\sqrt{44}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-1)={180}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb1e08c5-8191-51cb-828c-4e1bf4d18edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269075} {:answer/id #uuid "c48d61db-8a7b-58a9-baa3-b45f0e2b2e24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{77}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269076} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe43b6a-8e20-5aa9-b47c-1e0b409544b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{86}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269077} {:answer/id #uuid "a8481d0e-1847-5899-a263-24206ff622f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{91}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269078} {:answer/id #uuid "f68369eb-d5b2-597a-8ad3-4e02ef54893c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fe43b6a-8e20-5aa9-b47c-1e0b409544b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{86}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269077} :answer-field/id #uuid "4237779a-fb1d-5aae-9935-ca22c819fe5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269074}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16a09fd3-be95-51b4-b0ac-0c24039ae9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-101511" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,1)$, $B(3,1,-2)$, and $C(-1,1,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,1,-2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}})≈{86}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b8bdbb-40f0-5e9c-9af6-75ad034239f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{116.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269082} {:answer/id #uuid "8c46e53c-d1ff-5dc9-ad5b-7d8ca4d94a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{111.1}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269083} {:answer/id #uuid "23bbb5d2-e5e3-5cee-9ce1-e977f27b0c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{122.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269084} {:answer/id #uuid "047be692-7ec1-5921-9e3e-a096d5ab0960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{113.8}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269085} {:answer/id #uuid "00c34ec0-c0f2-5eaa-bd8f-92c1fa6ac6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120.9}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28b8bdbb-40f0-5e9c-9af6-75ad034239f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{116.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269082} :answer-field/id #uuid "f467919b-d9c3-556d-b9c6-eb60fabcc3ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269081}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "852d0fcb-212d-5f7f-bb3f-afcaa190e7c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-101514" :question/problem "Given that $a\\cdot b=-10$, find the angle between $a=⟨-4t,3t⟩$ and $b=⟨2,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $a\\cdot b=-10$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-10 \\\\ (-4t)\\cdot 2+3t\\cdot 1 & =-10 \\\\ -8t+3t & =-10 \\\\ -5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨-4(2),\\,3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10}{\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{10\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}})≈{116.6}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33d889d7-3053-5698-b65c-fe5ae9aa07f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75.22}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269089} {:answer/id #uuid "bf85c120-7483-5553-bdcd-a44069470789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{78.55}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269090} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6a7436-5d40-5ead-afe9-8fc3f33b83ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{70.99}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269091} {:answer/id #uuid "08336714-fd00-56fc-9883-ef766d26fd89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269092} {:answer/id #uuid "7934f66e-abaa-5481-ab13-a79e21a04132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80.44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7934f66e-abaa-5481-ab13-a79e21a04132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80.44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269093} :answer-field/id #uuid "69c601c3-8547-5f8b-8af3-b0698702489b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269088}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8fc7cf1b-c116-59a4-83f2-94ca1412ae63" :question/math-academy-id "q-101520" :question/problem "Consider the points $D(t,5,3)$, $E({t}^{2},2,t)$ and $F(t+3,{t}^{2},1).$ Find $∠EDF$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=6.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $D$, $E$, $F$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d=⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩,\\,e=⟨{t}^{2},\\,2,\\,t⟩,\\,f=⟨t+3,\\,{t}^{2},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△DEF$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠EDF=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/c9cfb3e84e6f76d243125f2a09246b2a1300a0134e71359bb2b528082f064f93.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,2,\\,t⟩-⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,-3,\\,t-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =⟨t+3,\\,{t}^{2},\\,1⟩-⟨t,\\,5,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,{t}^{2}-5,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=6$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =6 \\\\ ({t}^{2}-t)\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot ({t}^{2}-5)+(t-3)\\cdot (-2) & =6 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-3t-3{t}^{2}+15-2t+6 & =6 \\\\ -5t+21 & =6 \\\\ -5t & =-15 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨{3}^{2}-3,-3,3-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-3,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨3,{3}^{2}-5,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}}{|\\overset{\\to }{DE}||\\overset{\\to }{DF}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{145}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{145}})≈{80.44}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269094 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d53a02b-b33e-51dd-8ab2-e9af5a421db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269096} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f9b012-c354-5d6e-9581-72bdf697d50f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{67}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269097} {:answer/id #uuid "4d60903b-6a7a-53d2-83bb-a4aa0851a070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269098} {:answer/id #uuid "4a098196-3c16-5eab-ba4d-21e17c7dbf00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{62}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269099} {:answer/id #uuid "f3aaf77e-f91e-5eec-80e8-ad79e8adb224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{59}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3f9b012-c354-5d6e-9581-72bdf697d50f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{67}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269097} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae427d9-2381-531f-87a7-c13fc1fb292e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269095}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1d872083-4e1c-5f3c-8347-aaf05eb74faf" :question/math-academy-id "q-125079" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(t,1,1)$, $B(3t,1,3)$ and $C(3,-2,{t}^{2}).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=4.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨t,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,1,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨3,\\,-2,\\,{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,1,\\,3⟩-⟨t,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,{t}^{2}⟩-⟨t,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3-t,\\,-3,\\,{t}^{2}-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=4$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =4 \\\\ 2t\\cdot (3-t)+0\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1) & =4 \\\\ 6t-2{t}^{2}+0+2{t}^{2}-2 & =4 \\\\ 6t-2 & =4 \\\\ 6t & =6 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,0,2⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨3-1,\\,3,\\,{1}^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{26}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{26}})≈{67}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae483db5-b844-59a3-abdf-beb3a53c5b70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64.6^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102370} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d3d26f-e1a2-5d91-9a7b-2f6e6445bd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "146.9^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102371} {:answer/id #uuid "dba0727c-6ab5-5589-913c-df2fce9167b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102372} {:answer/id #uuid "0783952b-22ef-5807-9369-f5fbfd704078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16.2^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102373} {:answer/id #uuid "6df49944-a6f8-5e4f-b82e-ad0d988d929f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.2^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae483db5-b844-59a3-abdf-beb3a53c5b70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64.6^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102370} :answer-field/id #uuid "b604b328-bb74-5942-8fd6-e086ec6b1b12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102369}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23a2df8e-948e-5b82-a7dc-fb5d528e3df5" :question/math-academy-id "q-18320" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFind the angle between $a = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 6+7\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{7}^{2}}\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{53}\\cdot \\sqrt{37}} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{1961}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{1961}})≈{64.6}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f7ff979-0782-51f8-ae4c-e18fb9d4d5b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269103} {:answer/id #uuid "e2865549-e3e9-581d-a55a-ef32150ac727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45.78}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269104} {:answer/id #uuid "501c6352-5d0e-5e87-bb7c-213d1c3cb56e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{32.88}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269105} {:answer/id #uuid "93c83d58-c4a8-534d-8989-eefb264493b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{36.87}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269106} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf16502-501f-5824-9c6f-c47d81fd150d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{33.74}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93c83d58-c4a8-534d-8989-eefb264493b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{36.87}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269106} :answer-field/id #uuid "a29ee5d9-bc93-5485-87d5-05b0c023178b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269102}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a459d13d-af6a-517a-94fc-980ae982205d" :question/math-academy-id "q-19027" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{20}\\cdot \\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{4}{5})≈{36.87}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8afbfb09-b22c-5fb4-ad63-9b272b5b0f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{74.66}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269110} {:answer/id #uuid "8963ce6a-0bfd-5fd2-b165-d792ada55b90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82.28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269111} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6a8900-1583-5035-b877-a331a777d7a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79.76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269112} {:answer/id #uuid "5826b01a-a2bb-59f5-97f6-55db95fe21e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{94.32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269113} {:answer/id #uuid "6745ac4a-89a9-5753-84d7-9c7d0584dc63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6745ac4a-89a9-5753-84d7-9c7d0584dc63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269114} :answer-field/id #uuid "a854aaae-2f37-5309-b178-44153a0fe3f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de2bc7db-4647-58f0-bdd4-89b0098b6ec1" :question/math-academy-id "q-19036" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨4,-3,2⟩$ and $b=⟨3,4,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{29}\\cdot \\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{754}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{754}})≈{85.82}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2af7d00d-5eee-555a-9c9d-addb6f4e2953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7.84}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269117} {:answer/id #uuid "1c9fcf50-d78e-5968-97ce-3650cab4860b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{9.21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269118} {:answer/id #uuid "d0615396-aa63-5291-a7c9-bc4f6e1a54b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11.49}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269119} {:answer/id #uuid "6373f1ff-8af8-58d2-9b25-2bcc48548f47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15.36}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269120} {:answer/id #uuid "a84efaa8-d771-5a5e-b71c-c2a53b44a9ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35.92}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0615396-aa63-5291-a7c9-bc4f6e1a54b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11.49}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269119} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c79751-db81-5814-a47f-b1052c81c40b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9977a1dd-4a81-52ff-bede-89adf3e6a78e" :question/math-academy-id "q-19037" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{3\\sqrt{14}})≈{11.49}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed774057-02be-5493-896f-c9b973d6a63c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{132.4}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269124} {:answer/id #uuid "004c9eb0-5a71-5df8-b041-27504f9d73ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110.8}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269125} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c9fdee-1a62-5d99-b8a6-6f15b43fb29c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{92.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269126} {:answer/id #uuid "3644af28-f706-5f0f-9ae0-d5fc607f96c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{104.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269127} {:answer/id #uuid "18fbf17f-6676-5ef4-94f3-f5c84e4ee533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{84.7}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3644af28-f706-5f0f-9ae0-d5fc607f96c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{104.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269127} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbb7ddab-cbbf-5ec3-9438-35e2697ee7d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269123}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba4d9a12-1a1e-55c8-94d8-119632f1d338" :question/math-academy-id "q-19038" :question/problem "Given that $p\\cdot q=-5$, find the angle between $p=⟨4t,-2,t⟩$ and $q=⟨1,3,-3⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $p\\cdot q=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =-5 \\\\ 4t\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 3+t\\cdot (-3) & =-5 \\\\ 4t-6-3t & =-5 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨4(1),-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $p$ and $q$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,||\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{21}\\cdot \\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{399}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTHerefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{399}})≈{104.5}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269129 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16104c2f-285a-58e3-a912-1c5c32735793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{18}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269131} {:answer/id #uuid "d7796c45-683b-5992-8c9f-34c50eb36c28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269132} {:answer/id #uuid "551cfa18-cedc-5bbe-8306-3487d020644c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{112}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269133} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea035f0-6207-54f9-8514-fc252b0a6a65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269134} {:answer/id #uuid "48b4dd83-fc3a-5279-9506-b1c1c610adae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7796c45-683b-5992-8c9f-34c50eb36c28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269132} :answer-field/id #uuid "0865b498-b4a5-5b7f-ba31-8063a63b2589" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269130}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26ec9194-f492-518e-8975-e0a3b197c76c" :question/math-academy-id "q-19107" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,1,-1)$, $B(3,-2,2)$, and $C(-1,-2,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853ea703-1d96-539c-87e3-e34d3d095438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269138} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f223ca-0fea-5bae-8cdd-b11ad4571b15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{27}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269139} {:answer/id #uuid "12fb3ba3-823c-5cfc-b083-6ce78c505fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269140} {:answer/id #uuid "e05e7500-7274-5b9b-90bd-0b84dc643510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269141} {:answer/id #uuid "9a09a8bd-4160-5cba-b8e6-8131c8959abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e05e7500-7274-5b9b-90bd-0b84dc643510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269141} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4556650-d240-5520-9d69-8f8ef1163437" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269137}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e553e89a-b69b-5299-b9b3-9573916538d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-69831" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,1,2)$, $Q(1,3,2)$, and $R(4,5,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,1,2⟩,\\,q=⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,r=⟨4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,3,2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨4,5,-2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,4,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5})≈{63}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73d308c4-816e-53bb-9c5e-3a09bfaddfb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269145} {:answer/id #uuid "72673e86-c085-5291-8bec-166da72a0e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269146} {:answer/id #uuid "32c95188-10a9-5114-99b0-cb90db5d77b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269147} {:answer/id #uuid "84cd7a4c-ec32-59ce-a7d2-70ca0fd02759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269148} {:answer/id #uuid "d2487dac-0617-58ae-8a51-f5bdcd054680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73d308c4-816e-53bb-9c5e-3a09bfaddfb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269145} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f26f37a-46b8-5fce-81b3-84be685ab68e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269144}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09283c16-ce85-51a9-9e26-ee1e56005470" :question/math-academy-id "q-77159" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,4,1),$ $Q(3,4,2)$ and $R(3,3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P,$ $Q$ and $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,4,1⟩,\\,q=⟨3,4,2⟩,\\,r=⟨3,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨3,4,2⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨3,3,1⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})={60}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb9d024a-612a-5b88-b561-2eca5dd12c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269152} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee2a05a-ca70-5223-ba9e-36cd6fa08e55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269153} {:answer/id #uuid "6eaac85c-277b-51f1-baf6-a4d8434347b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269154} {:answer/id #uuid "a4eef7ee-ce27-568c-aa25-74f1486ec107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269155} {:answer/id #uuid "3f8ec3a5-7e51-5c63-9ee0-131bcdf218d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f8ec3a5-7e51-5c63-9ee0-131bcdf218d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269156} :answer-field/id #uuid "89db74db-3d63-59f5-b41d-544e3f33dabd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269151}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61191758-28d5-55a6-95f0-ed679272a908" :question/math-academy-id "q-77164" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(3t,t,4),$ $B(3t,4t,3)$ and $C(5t,t+1,5).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3t,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ 0\\cdot 2t+3t\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 3t-1 & =2 \\\\ 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,3,-1⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}})≈{75}^{∘}.\n$$"}]}
